  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Friday)\nIssued at 105 PM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nMild and dry afternoon on tap as upper level ridge builds in the \nwestern US. Drier weather and warming temps expected through the \nweekend as the ridge continues to build. With humidities dropping \ninto the upper teens to 20s tomorrow, elevated fire wx conditions \nmay develop over portions of northeastern WY and southwestern SD \nwhere breezy southwest winds will develop in the afternoon.\n\nUpper level flow becomes more southwesterly late in the weekend. \nClosed upper low makes its way onshore over southern CA by Sunday.\nThis system transforms to an open wave as treks northeastward \nacross the desert Southwest and the Rockies. It should pass to our\nsouth early in the week with the main impacts being breezy \nsoutheasterly winds across portions of our area Monday and \nTuesday. Temperatures next week will continue to be seasonably \nmild with highs in the 60s to 70s across much of the area.\n\nNext chances for precip arrive later next week as another trof \ndeepens across the western US, though it's still too far out to \ndetermine any specifics about precip chances or timing.",
